ry":{"type":"git","url":"git+https://github.com/sindresorhus/domify.git"},"description":"Turn a HTML string into DOM elements, cross-platform","maintainers":[{"name":"sindresorhus","email":"sindresorhus@gmail.com"}],"readme":"# domify\n\n> Turn a HTML string into DOM elements, cross-platform\n\n## Usage\n\nWorks out of the box in the browser:\n\n```js\nimport domify from 'domify';\n\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n\tconst element = domify('<p>Hello <em>there</em></p>');\n\tdocument.body.appendChild(element);\n});\n```\n\nYou can also run it in Node.js and other non-browser environments by passing a custom implementation of `document`:\n\n```js\nimport {JSDOM} from 'jsdom';\n\nconst jsdom = new JSDOM();\n\ndomify('<p>Hello <em>there</em></p>', jsdom.window.document);\n```\n\n**Note:** For browser-only use, prefer [`DOMParser.parseFromString()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DOMParser/parseFromString).\n","readmeFilename":"readme.md","users":{"ysk8":true,"zeke":true,"akiva":true,"stany":true,"allain":true,"h02e56":true,"joakin":true,"hzapata":true,"markoni":true,"nichoth":true,"parroit":true,"wenbing":true,"dexteryy":true,"erikvold":true,"hecto932":true,"jackvial":true,"jtavarez":true,"moimikey":true,"hellopath":true,"nomemires":true,"garrickajo":true,"kuzmicheff":true,"nickleefly":true,"tehmachine":true,"jondashkyle":true,"tunnckocore":true}}